# Three-surface parity (mandatory)

כל פיצ'ר חדש או שיפור לפיצ'ר קיים באפליקציה הראשית חייב להיבחן ולתמוך גם באפליקציית העובדים
ובאפליקציית הקבלנים, כאשר הפיצ'ר רלוונטי להם ויש להם הרשאות מתאימות.

Every new feature or improvement in the main app must be evaluated for the **employee app** and the
**contractor app**, and supported there when it is relevant and the user holds matching permissions.

## Rules

1. **Default = parity.** The same permission gives the same capability on every surface.
2. **No app-type restrictions.** Never gate a capability on `employeeApp` / `external` alone. A blanket
   restriction that blocks an authorized user is fixed with a proper capability permission - never by
   opening unrestricted access.
3. **Differences only by permission or a documented essential need** (for example: a provider web login
   employees/contractors do not have; a contractor has no read grant on raw project folders). Document every
   intentional limitation next to the feature (matrix doc, code comment on the resolver).
4. **Share, do not copy.** One component, one use-case, one server action. Surface wrappers wire transport only
   (route, browse actions, session kind) and must not decide capabilities. Derive capability flags in one pure
   resolver (see `src/modules/infra-mapping/domain/permissions.ts`).
5. **Security stays intact.** RLS, organization isolation, project / vendor / location scoping are never bypassed;
   permissions are never auto-granted; employees and contractors need no personal cloud account (uploads go to
   the organization storage through the system, within permissions).
6. **Check all three surfaces on every relevant change** and add focused tests for the permission rule and the
   isolation (not wide suites).

Reference matrix: `docs/product/infra-three-surface-parity-matrix.md`.
